## 5. What Gets Dropped (and What the Copilot Replaces)

| Current Feature | What Happens | Notes |
|----------------|-------------|-------|
| OpenAI Agents SDK | **Removed entirely** | No `agents` dependency |
| System prompts (`prompts.py`) | **Moved to tool descriptions** | Copilot reads tool descriptions as its "schema" |
| 30-turn agent loop | **Copilot handles** | Copilot decides when to call which tool |
| Recipe extraction (`extractor.py`) | **Dropped (v1)** | Can be added back later as a separate tool |
| Recipe execution (`runner.py`) | **Could keep as a tool** | `execute_recipe` with params |
| Dynamic tool naming (`middleware.py`) | **Dropped** | Not needed — tools have fixed names |
| Turn tracking (`progress.py`) | **Dropped** | Copilot manages its own turns |
| Tracing (`tracing.py`) | **Optional keep** | Can trace individual tool calls |
| `X-Target-URL` headers | **Become tool parameters** | Each call passes URL explicitly |
| `return_directly` flag | **Dropped** | Copilot always sees results |

