## 7. Copilot Workflow (What the User Sees)

The copilot orchestrates the same steps the embedded agent used to do internally:

```
User: "What are the top 10 hotels in Bangkok by rating?"

Copilot thinking:
  1. Call fetch_schema(
       target_url="https://api.example.com/graphql",
       api_type="graphql"
     )
     → Gets schema: hotels(city: String!) -> [Hotel { id, name, rating, ... }]

  2. Call execute_graphql(
       query='{ hotels(city: "Bangkok") { name rating } }',
       target_url="https://api.example.com/graphql"
     )
     → Gets results, stored as table "data"

  3. Call sql_query(
       sql="SELECT name, rating FROM data ORDER BY rating DESC LIMIT 10"
     )
     → Gets top 10

  4. Formats and returns to user
```

### REST Example

```
User: "List active users from the admin API"

Copilot thinking:
  1. Call fetch_schema(
       target_url="https://admin.example.com/openapi.json",
       api_type="rest"
     )
     → Gets endpoints: GET /users(status?) -> User[]

  2. Call execute_rest(
       method="GET",
       path="/users",
       query_params={"status": "active"},
       base_url="https://admin.example.com"
     )
     → Gets results, stored as table "data"

  3. Call sql_query(
       sql="SELECT id, name, email FROM data ORDER BY name"
     )
     → Gets sorted list

  4. Formats and returns to user
```

